It succeeds the Agentic Workspace Starter Kit, whose history stays reachable in
this repository at tags v0.1.0 and v0.2.0 under the same license.

Context Fabric is also the successor to the DMod Context Fabric component, which
remains in service while this framework is built. Where both are in play, the
earlier one is referred to as the DMod Context Fabric component; Context Fabric
unqualified means this framework.

This repository is public so that a Nava program can read the framework without
an access request. Every organization, system, person, and secret reference
committed here is fictional or a placeholder; real facts live in a
practitioner's own documents root, which is outside this repository.

The planning and research documents that produced this framework are
deliberately not published here. They carry internal program and system detail
that the framework itself does not, and they stay in the maintainer's local
tree.
